quran[8]{c,v,t}:
  7,23,"They said: ‘Our Lord! We have wronged ourselves. And if You do not forgive us and have mercy on us, we shall surely be among the losers.’"
  7,24,He said: ‘Descend! Some of you (will be) enemies of one another. And there will be a residence for you on the earth and a provision for some time.’
  7,25,"He said: ‘Therein you shall live, and therein you shall die, and from there you shall be raised (on the Day of Resurrection).’"
  7,26,"O Children of Adam! We have indeed sent down to you garments to cover your private parts and for adornment. Yet the garment of God-consciousness—that is the best. That is one of Allah’s signs, so perhaps they may become mindful (of advice)."
  7,27,"O Children of Adam! Let not Satan tempt you (too) as he brought your parents out of Paradise, stripping them of their garments to expose their private parts to them. Indeed, he sees you—he and his tribe (members)—from where you cannot see them. Indeed, We have made the satans allies of those who do not believe."
  7,28,"Whenever they commit a shameful act, they say: ‘We found our forefathers practising it, and Allah has commanded us to do it.’ Say: ‘Indeed, Allah does not command indecency. Do you attribute to Allah what you do not know?’"
  7,29,"Say: ‘My Lord commands justice. So set your faces (towards Him) on every occasion (and at every place) of prayer. And worship Him, devoting your obedience sincerely to Him. Just as He originated you, so shall you return (to life again).’"
  7,30,"A group He has guided, and a group deserves to go astray—they have taken devils as their guardians instead of Allah, and they think they are guided."
